{'symbol': 'EXC', 'date': '2022-06-22 11:00:00', 'title': 'COMED AND UIC SAFEGUARD NEARLY 4,000 ACRES IN NORTHERN ILLINOIS AS POLLINATOR HABITATS', 'text': "CHICAGO--(BUSINESS WIRE)--COMED TODAY JOINED THE UNIVERSITY OF ILLINOIS CHICAGO (UIC) IN ANNOUNCING IT HAS REACHED A NEW MILESTONE IN POLLINATOR HABITAT CONSERVATION, WITH NEARLY 4,000 ACRES OF POWERLINE CORRIDOR LAND NOW DEEMED POLLINATOR HABITATS. EFFORTS TO CONSERVE POLLINATOR HABITATS ARE PART OF COMED'S PLEDGE TO PRESERVE 11,700 ACRES OF UTILITY OWNED LAND BY 2025 FOR HABITATS THAT SUPPORT THE MONARCH BUTTERFLY, WHICH IS AT RISK OF EXTINCTION. THE ANNOUNCEMENT COMES IN TIME FOR NATIONAL PO"}